/*
 * MemoryExpander — expands memory-related operations into YIL values.
 *
 * The MemoryExpander lowers high-level memory constructs into concrete
 * YILValue and YILInstr nodes. It handles:
 *
 *   - address-of operations(&),
 *   - dereferencing(*),
 *   - reference creation,
 *   - lazy value construction,
 *   - copying of slices, maps, and tuples,
 *   - mover semantics for class instances,
 *   - future spawning,
 *   - aliasing and copier/dereferencer operators.
 *
 * It ensures correct pointer depth handling, avoids double-addressing,
 * and guarantees that heavy operations(copy, spawn) are executed only once
 * by registering unique values.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::lint::expander::value::memory
 * @File: ymirc/lint/expander/value/memory.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-06-23
